        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d7b27fa4-9d8e-57b2-87e7-a973767ac1f2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Haunted Mansion, The Greatest Game Ever Played, My Dinner with Andre, The Princess Bride, Toy Story franchise, The Incredibles\n- People: Wallace Shawn, Mark Frost, Louis Malle, Harry Vardon, Francis Ouimet\n- Places: Disney theme park attraction\n- Topics: film adaptation, screenplay, voice acting\n\nFacts:\n- The Haunted Mansion is a 2003 American fantasy comedy horror film based on the Disney theme park attraction of the same name.\n- Wallace Shawn played Wally Shawn in Louis Malle's 1981 comedy-drama My Dinner with Andre.\n- Wallace Shawn played Vizzini in The Princess Bride in 1987.\n- Mark Frost adapted the screenplay for The Greatest Game Ever Played from his book The Greatest Game Ever Played: Harry Vardon, Francis Ouimet, and the Birth of Modern Golf.\n- Wallace Shawn played Ezra in The Haunted Mansion.\n- Wallace Shawn voiced Rex in the Toy Story franchise.\n- Wallace Shawn voiced Gilbert Huph in The Incredibles in 2004.\n- Wallace Shawn voiced Calico in a 2010 film with an unspecified title.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2e8a2c20-c152-5b5a-be4e-f3cd72f7d4dc",
        "text": "Page: The Haunted Mansion (film). Sentence: The Haunted Mansion is a 2003 American fantasy comedy horror film based on the Disney theme park attraction of the same name.\nPage: The Greatest Game Ever Played. Sentence: The film's screenplay was adapted by Mark Frost from his book, \"The Greatest Game Ever Played: Harry Vardon, Francis Ouimet, and the Birth of Modern Golf\".\nPage: Wallace Shawn. Sentence: His film roles have included those of Wally Shawn in the Louis Malle-directed comedy-drama \"My Dinner with Andre\" (1981), Vizzini in \"The Princess Bride\" (1987), Ezra in \"The Haunted Mansion\", providing the voice of Rex in the \"Toy Story\" franchise, providing the voice of Gilbert Huph in \"The Incredibles\" (2004), and providing the voice of Calico in \"\" (2010).",
